# Project Config of home:jmbriccola:porthole on build.opensuse.org -- what is
# pasted into the project's "Project Config" tab, kept here so the repository
# says what the build service is doing and why.
#
# The spec builds from the vendored crate tree (its Source1) only under
# `--with vendor`. OBS builders have no network, so on OBS it is always on.
# The Debian packages need nothing here: debian/rules goes offline by itself
# when the source package carries vendor/.
#
# Not in this file, because it lives in the repository definitions rather
# than in the project config: Debian_13 builds against Debian:13/standard *and*
# Debian:13/backports. Debian 13 ships rustc 1.85, this workspace needs 1.87,
# and trixie-backports carries a newer one.
#
# Debian 13 has two packages that answer to libjpeg-dev, which OBS reported
# as needed by libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-dev and libtiff-dev: libjpeg-dev itself,
# which depends on libjpeg62-turbo-dev, and libjpeg62-turbo-dev, which
# provides it. apt picks the real package without asking; OBS refuses to pick
# and calls the build unresolvable, which is what the first upload got
# (2026-09-11). Naming the one apt would pick keeps OBS and apt in step.
Prefer: libjpeg-dev

Macros:
%_with_vendor 1
:Macros
